{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>You have given</b> — They desire that we not see good, but I was glad when I saw them in good." "And the meaning of <b>you have given</b> — for You have given me a good heart to desire good for all. And Rabbi Judah ben Balaam said: for it is read [as though] their grain is turned, and the truth is [that] it is read דְּגָנָם וְתִירוֹשָׁם. And there is no need to reverse things spoken by the holy spirit."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {1 "The phrase מעת דגנם הפוך is obscure; possibly corrupt or elliptical. Ben Balaam apparently references a tradition that 'their grain and their wine' (דגנם ותירושם) has been transposed or inverted in some reading tradition. Rendered hyper-literally without smoothing."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:26:25.981448738Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}